## OPERATOR ANNOTATION (host, 2026-07-14) — WHY THIS RUN FAILED, AND WHY IT MATTERS
##
## This run used the DEFAULT macOS $TMPDIR = /var/folders/... , which is a SYMLINK
## to /private/var/folders/... . Under that prefix, DIRECTION 2 (the plan's chosen
## fix) and DIRECTION 3's reads BOTH FAIL with the identical error the bug produces:
##     fatal: not a git repository: (null)
##
## The same script, same Docker, same mount shape, run under a NON-symlinked prefix
## (/Users/...) PASSES all of DIRECTION 2 and 3 — see p5-docker-container-git.out.
##
## FINDING (VERIFIED, executed both ways): PATH-IDENTITY MOUNTING IS NOT SYMLINK-SAFE.
## If the host .git path traverses a symlink, the container resolves a different
## absolute path than the .git pointer file records, and git fails EXACTLY as it does
## in the unfixed case. The implementation MUST canonicalize (realpath) the host path
## before constructing the mount, and the fail-loud detector MUST compare CANONICAL
## paths -- otherwise the fix silently no-ops on any symlinked checkout and looks
## identical to the defect it was shipped to eliminate.
